  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/38c14748-884b-4c02-9e71-dbff8f4675ca.png\" style=\"width:3.09375in;height:2.17361in\" /><br />Reflection of <math><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> about line <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3,2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></math><br />Equation of the line <math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is the same as line <math><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math> equation of the line <math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>x</mi></math> and the equation of the line <math><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi></math> is <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>x</mi></math>.<br />Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math> are the angle bisectors of the lines <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Now, angle bisectors of&nbsp;<math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
